---
import ContentLayout from "../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import ObfuscatedLink from "../components/ObfuscatedLink.astro";
import { email } from "../constants";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Pearce Labs"
  description="Terms of service for Pearce Labs."
  robots="noindex, follow">
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p
    class="mt-1 mb-8 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-stone-500 uppercase">
    Effective May 20, 2026
  </p>

  <h2>Services</h2>
  <p>
    Pearce Labs provides custom software development, AI implementation, data
    engineering, web development, and technology consulting services. The scope
    of services for each engagement is defined in a separate project agreement
    or statement of work.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <p>
    Services are generally invoiced on a recurring, per-project, or retainer
    basis. Specific payment terms and conditions for each engagement are defined
    in a separate project agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
  <p>
    Intellectual property terms and conditions for each engagement are defined
    in a separate project agreement. Pearce Labs retains ownership of any
    general tools, frameworks, or know-how developed independently of the
    project.
  </p>

  <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    Both parties agree to keep the other's confidential information private.
    Client information will not be disclosed to third parties except where
    reasonably necessary to carry out the engagement — including use of
    third-party tools and services such as email clients, project management
    platforms, communication tools, and other software used in the ordinary
    course of delivering the work. Any such third parties are expected to handle
    information responsibly and in accordance with their own privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>
    Pearce Labs' total liability for any claim arising from an engagement is
    limited to the fees paid for that engagement. In no event will Pearce Labs
    be liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Commonwealth of Virginia. Any
    disputes will be resolved in the courts of Fairfax County, Virginia.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <ObfuscatedLink href={`mailto:${email}`} label={email} />
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
